EVENTSOUND(1)                   User Commands                    EVENTSOUND(1)

NAME
       eventsound - play a system event sound

SYNOPSIS
       eventsound NAME [-w] [-t SECONDS] [-v VOLUME] [-q]
       eventsound --list

DESCRIPTION
       eventsound asks the audio service, audiod(1), to play the system  sound
       NAME, the  file  /usr/share/sounds/likeos/NAME.wav:  startup  when  the
       desktop starts, logout when it ends, shutdown, login,  notify,  error,
       volume, and whatever else has been put there.

       Only the name travels to the service,  which  opens  the  file  itself.
       Names are a single word of letters, digits, '-', '_' and '.',  at  most
       31 characters, and can never reach outside that directory.  A  trailing
       .wav is ignored.

       eventsound is made for scripts and is careful never to make  one  fail:
       when the audio service is not running, there is no  sound  card,  event
       sounds are switched off in the service's configuration,  or  the  sound
       does not exist, it exits with status 0 without printing anything.  Only
       a malformed name or option is an error. Without -w it returns  as  soon
       as the service has accepted the request, so a script does not wait  for
       the sound to finish.

       The whole run is bounded: connecting and asking  take  at  most  a  few
       seconds, and with -w the wait ends after the timeout even if the  sound
       has not finished (it still plays to its end). A  shut-down  that  plays
       its sound with -w can therefore never hang on it.

OPTIONS
       -w, --wait
              Return only once the sound has been played, or when the  timeout
              runs out.

       -t, --timeout SECONDS
              The longest wait, 0..3600 seconds; 0 waits as long as it  takes.
              Default 10.

       -v, --volume N
              Volume of this sound, 0..100 (default 100), on top of the master
              volume.

       -q, --quiet
              No error messages at all.

       -l, --list
              List the sounds in /usr/share/sounds/likeos with  their  length,
              and exit.

       -h, --help
              A summary of the options.

EXAMPLES
       eventsound startup                 when a desktop has finished loading
       eventsound logout                  as the desktop session ends
       eventsound notify -v 50
       make && eventsound notify || eventsound error
       eventsound --list

EXIT STATUS
       0      The sound was handed to the service -- or could not be,  because
              there is no service, no sound card or no such sound.

       2      A malformed name or a bad option, or the  service  rejected  the
              name as invalid.

FILES
       /usr/share/sounds/likeos/*.wav
              The system sounds (48 kHz, 16-bit stereo WAV).

       /etc/audiod.conf
              event_sounds=no switches all event sounds off.

       /var/run/audiod/socket
              The audio service's socket.

SEE ALSO
       audioplay(1), audioctl(1), audiod(1)

